         <td style="font-weight: bold; font-size: 10pt;" background="/images/bg_heading_blue_01.jpg"><center><b>Nyplid mentioned by the Historian of Freeport</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
		 <td>                            
	                                   

	    <table border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0>
		  <tr><td><font color="00dd00">Submitted by:</td><td><font color="00dd00">Talis Atanatar</td></tr>
        </table>
	  <br>
	  <br>


          Hail and Well meet fellow Norrathians,<br>
          <br>
          Allow me to introduce myself I am Azarr Windtree Mage of the Mysts and member of the Great Atani Guild. I come here to inform you all of a great saga just begone. The saga began one night hence as I traveled through West Freeport, I happened apon a small band of my fellow Atani at the Theatre who sat quitely listening to a man named Hicor, so being the curious mage I am, I to stopped to listen to the Hicor's tale. He spoke of his friend Nyplid, who on the very day of his wedding had been manhandled and spirited away. Nicor told of how he had investigated Nyplid's disapearence. His investigation had of course begone were Nyplid had last been seen and soon came to believe that the dark races of Norrath may of had something to do with Nyplid's disapearence. Though he found no strong clues he did find a note posted in one of the local taverns that spoke of a Shadow from another realm. The Shadow could not come into our realm nor could he take a person from this realm to his. Yet the Shadow had followers here in Norrath, ones of the dark races. Two of which the names are known, Drodak a Troll and Androdameia a Shdowknight. Turning up know other clues, Nicor decided to investagate the sewers of Freeport as it is rumored that the dark races inhabit them at times. Nicor said he began his search in the sewers and came apon a Darkelf, but though questions many times the Darkelf only ignored Nicor. After more investigation of the sewers he had come apon a piece of tatered cloth, the cloth had strange symbols as some sort of writing. He himself could not translate it to the fullest yet know that the cloth had something to do with the Shadow.<br>
          <br>
          We had all sat quitely listening to the occurance of poor Nyplid's kidnapping and of the search for him when Hicor asked that who among us would help to locate Nyplid and return him safely home. Out of the Atani that were assembled there four responed I being one of them. The others were Granaut A dwarven cleric who liked his ale, Nacacia a halfelf rogue, whos bueaty hides her deadly skills, and lastly Lowelf a druid, a blessing to know. After the four agreed to help, Hicor handed me the tatered cloth and told us to seek out a friend in Felwithe named Delcaraa, but that she might be hard to see as her mother was sick and that she had left her post as Cleric for the fireworks company Kaboom to tend to her, but we might seek out Cahboom who also worked for the comapny and he might aid us to find Delacaraa. Hicor did warn us not to let Cahboom see the Cloth as he would destroy it, why I am not sure. Hicor then left after thanking us for the help we offered. The four of us sat a moment and talking about what to do I, Nacacia and Granaut decided to set sail on the next boat that left for Faydwer. Lowelf decided he would go alone, as most druid seem to be loners most of the time, but he would keep us informed if he found out anything. We arrived shortly at Faydwer and headed to Felwithe, at the great wizard spires we meet the Gnome Kahboom who was interested in hiring our dwarven cleric friend as a replacement for Delcaraa until she could return to work, of which Granaut agreed, "so if by chance you are in Faydwer and here a loud boom know that Dwarven ale and fireworks do not mix well." After talking to Cahboom he agreed to lead us to were Delcaraa lived, apon ariving and introducing our selves she asked that the others leave and of course I asked that Cahboom leave as well so that we could talk in private, but unknown to Delcaraa, Nacacia had used your stealth to sneak back in. I then took out the tatered cloth from my backpack and showed it to Delacaraa, she stood back in amazment. Asked if she might have the cloth to investigate it. I agreed, she took the cloth and said that it would take at least a week befor she could tell me more of what it was and perhaps how it fit into Nyplids disapearence. We left her to her studies "I was thankful to get rid of that piece of cloth if made me fell very uneasy holding on to it."<br>
          <br>
          Knowing how well my drawven friend likes his ale we decided to head to the local tavern in Felwithe for a few rounds and some discussion of the events. We all drank to the day and to the hopefully safe return of Nyplid, not knowing what the future would hold. We all agreed on meeting one week hence to find out what Delacaraa had to say. I look forward to what lies ahead.<br>
          <br>
          Azarr Windtree<br>
          Mage of the Mysts Azarr Windtree<br>
